      "html": "<p>Hatchetfishes belong to very few species of fish that are able to fly. A hatchetfish on the run jumps out of the water and uses the pectoral fins just like wings. So these tiny species, only 5-6 cm long, can jump several meters. The typical hatchet-shaped belly is also an adaptation for flying, because it is needed for the necessary musculature.</p><ul><li>Origin: Colombia</li><li>Available size: 5-6 cm</li></ul>"
